This file holds the ASCII-armored PUBLIC PGP keys of swift-java maintainers who are
allowed to sign release tags. It is imported by .github/workflows/publish-release.yml,
which then runs `git verify-tag` against the pushed tag before publishing anything.

This is NOT the artifact-signing key. The artifact-signing PRIVATE key used to sign
published jars/poms lives only in the ORG_GRADLE_PROJECT_SIGNINGKEY GitHub secret and
is never committed here.

To add yourself as a trusted release signer:
  1. gpg --export --armor YOUR_KEY_ID >> .github/release-signers.asc
  2. Open a pull request with the change and get it reviewed and merged.

Until this file contains at least one key, no tag can be verified, so
publish-release.yml fails closed by design.
